{"name":"Hawaiian Vacation","hex":"#77cabd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vacation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An extended trip or journey away from home for rest or pleasure. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An extended period of leisure time away from work or school."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend or take a vacation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hawaiian Vacation","blocks":[{"text":"Toy Story Toons: Hawaiian Vacation is a 2011 American animated short film produced by Pixar Animation Studios and directed by Gary Rydstrom. The first entry in the Toy Story Toons series, the short features characters from the Toy Story films and takes place after the events of Toy Story 3. It premiered in theaters with Pixar's Cars 2, and was included on the film's home video release."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/63/Hawaiian_Vacation_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawaiian_Vacation","wikidata":"Q2457085"},{"title":"Vacation","blocks":[{"text":"A vacation or holiday is either a leave of absence from a regular job or school or an instance of leisure travel away from home. People often take a vacation during specific holiday observances or for specific festivals or celebrations. Vacations are often spent with friends or family. Vacations may include a specific trip or journey, usually for the purpose of recreation or tourism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Vacation_Village_at_Weston_Pool%2C_Weston%2C_Florida_February_24%2C_2022_B.jpg/330px-Vacation_Village_at_Weston_Pool%2C_Weston%2C_Florida_February_24%2C_2022_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vacation","wikidata":"Q116213"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wik